si: A module for parsing, converting, and formatting physical quantities expressed 
with the International System of Units.

- Repository: https://codeberg.org/swonky/hare-si.git

=== Examples ===
	
- Defining quantities using predefined constants:

	const distance = si::quantity { 
		unit = si::METRE, 
		value = 1500.0,
	};
	const duration = si::quantity { 
		unit = si::SECOND, 
		value = 120.0 
	};

- Performing arithmetic with quantities:

	const speed = si::divq(distance, duration);
	assert(speed.value == 12.5);

- Defining your own derived dimensions, units, and quantities:

	const pressure  = dimension { 
		mass = 1,
		length = -1, 
		time = -2,
		... 
	}; 
	const pascal = unit { 
		dim = pressure,
		scale = 1.0,
	};
	const atmospheric_pressure  = quantity { 
		unit = pascal,
		value = 101325.0,
	};

- Parsing ([[strp]]) and formatting ([[strf]]) strings:

	const acceleration = si::strp("20 m/s^2") as si::quantity;

	const output = si::strf(acceleration, "km*s^-2") as str;
	>> 0.02 km⋅s⁻²

	const output = si::strf(
		acceleration,
		"km/s^2",
		prec=3,
		notation=si::E,
		encoding=si::ASCII,
	) as str;
	>> 2.00e-02 km/s^2

=== Supported units ===

All symbols are case sensitive unless otherwise indicated.

Decimal prefix symbols [symbol=exponent]

- [[QUETTA]] (Q) = 1e30
- [[RONNA]] (R) = 1e27
- [[YOTTA]] (Y) = 1e24
- [[ZETTA]] (Z) = 1e21
- [[EXA]] (E) = 1e18
- [[PETA]] (P) = 1e15
- [[TERA]] (T) = 1e12
- [[GIGA]] (G) = 1e9
- [[MEGA]] (M) = 1e6
- [[KILO]] (k) = 1e3
- [[HECTO]] (h) = 1e2
- [[DECA]] (da) = 1e1
- [[DECI]] (d) = 1e-1
- [[CENTI]] (c) = 1e-2
- [[MILLI]] (m) = 1e-3
- [[MICRO]] (µ) = 1e-6
- [[NANO]] (n) = 1e-9
- [[PICO]] (p) = 1e-12
- [[FEMTO]] (f) = 1e-15
- [[ATTO]] (a) = 1e-18
- [[ZEPTO]] (z) = 1e-21
- [[YOCTO]] (y) = 1e-24
- [[RONTO]] (r) = 1e-27
- [[QUECTO]] (q) = 1e-30

Notes:
- Formatted ASCII output for [[MICRO]] uses 'LATIN SMALL LETTER U (U+0075)'
- Formattted UTF-8 output for [[MICRO]] uses 'GREEK SMALL LETTER MU (U+03BC)'.
- Parser for [[MICRO]] also accepts 'MICRO SIGN (U+00B5)'.

SI unit symbols

- [[AMPERE]]     (A)
- [[BECQUEREL]]  (Bq)
- [[CANDELA]]    (cd)
- [[COULOMB]]    (C)
- [[FARAD]]      (F)
- [[GRAM]]       (g)
- [[GRAY]]       (Gy)
- [[HENRY]]      (H)
- [[HERTZ]]      (Hz)
- [[JOULE]]      (J)
- [[KATAL]]      (kat)
- [[KELVIN]]     (K)
- [[LUMEN]]      (lm)
- [[LUX]]        (lx)
- [[METRE]]      (m)
- [[MOLE]]       (mol)
- [[NEWTON]]     (N)
- [[OHM]]        (ohm/Ω)
- [[PASCAL]]     (Pa)
- [[RADIAN]]     (rad)
- [[SECOND]]     (s)
- [[SIEMENS]]    (S)
- [[SIEVERT]]    (Sv)
- [[STERADIAN]]  (sr)
- [[TESLA]]      (T)
- [[VOLT]]       (V)
- [[WATT]]       (W)
- [[WEBER]]      (Wb)

Notes:
- UTF-8 output for [[OHM]] uses GREEK CAPITAL LETTER OMEGA (U+03A9).
- Parser for [[OHM]] also accepts OHM SIGN (U+2126).

Non-SI unit symbols [name=symbol]

- [[ASTRONOMICAL_UNIT]]  (au)      
- [[BEL]]                (B)       
- [[DALTON]]             (Da)      
- [[DAY]]                (d)       
- [[DEGREE]]             (deg/°)   
- [[DEGREE_CELSIUS]]     (degC/°C) 
- [[ELECTRONVOLT]]       (eV)      
- [[HECTARE]]            (ha)      
- [[HOUR]]               (h)       
- [[LITRE]]              (L)       
- [[MINUTE]]             (min)     
- [[NEPER]]              (Np)      
- [[TONNE]]              (t)       

Notes:
- Logarithmic units [[BEL]] and [[NEPER]] do not currently support conversion.
- Formatted UTF-8 outputs for [[DEGREE]] use DEGREE SIGN (U+00B0).
- Formatted output for '[[LITRE]] uses LATIN CAPITAL LETTER L (U+004C).
- Parser for [[LITRE]] also accepts LATIN SMALL LETTER L (U+006C).
